  model: "Enamel is laid down by ameloblasts on a timetable: first molar crowns start at birth and central incisors at about 3 to 4 months, so an illness at six months hits their ameloblasts mid-apposition and leaves a thin band of hypoplasia at the level being formed that month. Premolar crowns start mineralising at about 1.5 to 2.5 years, after the insult, so they are normal. The epithelium for a radicular cyst comes from Hertwig's root sheath: after it shapes the root it fragments into the epithelial rests of Malassez, which sit quietly in the ligament until inflammation from a necrotic pulp makes them proliferate and line a cavity."
